# Handling Failures 🔄

Network requests fail. APIs go down. Background tasks should automatically retry when they encounter transient errors.

Celery makes this easy.

```python_not
import requests

# Automatically retry up to 3 times, waiting 10 seconds between attempts
@app.task(bind=True, max_retries=3, default_retry_delay=10)
def fetch_data(self, url):
    try:
        response = requests.get(url)
        response.raise_for_status()
        return response.json()
    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as exc:
        # Tell celery to put the task back in the queue!
        raise self.retry(exc=exc)
```
